      howItWorksInternally: 'Prefixing a function call with `go` schedules a lightweight ~2KB goroutine onto the Go runtime. `sync.WaitGroup` maintains an atomic counter (`Add`, `Done`, `Wait`), and a channel (`chan T`) provides a synchronized queue for passing values between goroutines.',
      whyWeNeedIt: 'Sequential backends wait idly during network I/O (fetching user profile + permissions + billing one by one takes 30ms + 30ms + 30ms = 90ms; running them concurrently takes ~30ms).',
