      beginner: 'When you log into an app, the server gives your browser a digital badge called a **Bearer Token**. Every time your browser asks for private data, it shows that badge in an HTTP header: `Authorization: Bearer abc123xyz`.\n\n**Line-by-Line Syntax Walkthrough:**\n1. `const prefix = "Bearer "` — Defines the exact 7-character prefix required by RFC 6750.\n2. `if !strings.HasPrefix(authHeader, prefix) { return "", false }` — Safely rejects any header that does not start with `"Bearer "` (no slice index panics!).\n3. `tok := strings.TrimSpace(strings.TrimPrefix(authHeader, prefix))` — Removes `"Bearer "` and any extra spaces.\n4. `return tok, tok != ""` — Returns the token and `true` only if the remaining token is non-empty.',
      intermediate: 'Why does `strings.Split(h, " ")[1]` crash production servers? Because an attacker sending `Authorization: Basic` (no space) causes `strings.Split` to return a 1-element slice, triggering a runtime panic! `strings.HasPrefix` + `strings.TrimPrefix` is 100% panic-proof.',
