      whatIsIt: 'The foundational guide to Go unit testing: designing pure functions and testing multiple inputs and edge cases systematically using a table of test cases.',
      howItWorksInternally: 'Go\'s `testing` package runs any `func TestXxx(t *testing.T)` in `*_test.go` files. By defining a slice of test cases and iterating with `t.Run(tc.name, ...)`, you test 10 edge cases with a single 5-line assertion loop.',
      whyWeNeedIt: 'Untested backend code breaks silently when edge cases (like extra spaces or mixed case in article titles) hit production.',
