      diagram: '[Terminal: pwd / cd / mkdir] -> [git init & git commit] -> [go mod init example.com/app] -> [main.go] -> [go run .]',
      whatIsIt: 'The essential developer workflow combining the command-line terminal, Git version control, and the Go toolchain (go mod init, go run, go build, go test).',
      howItWorksInternally: 'When you run "go run .", the Go toolchain parses go.mod to resolve your module root, compiles all .go files in package main into a temporary native machine-code binary, and executes func main().',
      whyWeNeedIt: 'Backend engineers build, test, and deploy services through the CLI and automated CI pipelines rather than GUI buttons.',
      whyPreferred: 'Go includes a complete, zero-configuration toolchain (compiler, formatter gofmt, linter go vet, and test runner go test) out of the box.',
      whenToUse: 'At the start of every new Go repository or microservice.',
