      beginner: 'The Terminal is a text-based way to talk to your computer: `pwd` shows your current folder, `cd` changes folders, and `mkdir` creates a new folder. `git init` starts a time-machine history for your code. `go mod init` creates a `go.mod` ID card for your Go project, and `func main()` inside `package main` is the front door where your program starts running.',
      intermediate: 'A Go workspace is anchored by `go.mod`. Executable commands declare `package main` and `func main()`, while reusable libraries declare package names matching their directory names. Separating pure functions from `main()` enables unit testing via `go test`.',
